Z||000000||2farnorth||09-20-2001||06:08 AM||||An 85 coupe with the front facia replaced with an aero one.  Does anyone have a diagram of what should up under the front facia.  I can see where things have been cut and modified, but none of my other Fieros are the aero type so I don't know what's supposed to be there.  Thanks.<P>Dave||||reg||5
Z||000001||FieroJoe||09-20-2001||10:19 AM||||Well, first please rephrase exactly what you're trying to say there!  Nothing should have been cut or modified in any way to put any fascia on any Fiero!  They all share the same bolt holes and everything.<P>So, judging by your post I can't tell if you're having a problem with the fascia not being lined up or if you are just concerned with the way it is mounted.  Like I said, its just a bolt on, for ALL Fieros.  ||||reg||1
Z||000002||2farnorth||09-20-2001||01:19 PM||||The front inner fenders were cut and modified because the aero facia is apparently wider at the wheel opening.  The whole underside of the facia is open and basically unsupported.  There isn't even an energy absorber (bumper) under it.  I can see that some black material was cut away from under side of the facia in front of the radiator.  The whole area from the black lip on the bottom of the facia is open all the way back to the radiator.<P>Dave||||reg||5
Z||000003||84Bill||09-20-2001||01:29 PM||||There is quite a bit odd stuff that goes up under the aero facia, all kinds of brackets and other parts including a lower spoiler at the rear of the facia and a few other odds and ends. It has  much more stuff than the boat nose does.||||reg||1
Z||000004||2farnorth||09-20-2001||04:22 PM||||That's what I was afraid of.  I was hoping that someone would an exploded parts diagram of it so I could see what all is missing.  I have a diagram like that for the "boat nose"<P>Thanks<P>Dave||||reg||9
